1
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:20,562
I'm not a spy.

2
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:23,897
I'm not some foreign student either,
I promise.

3
00:00:23,898 --> 00:00:25,525
I've never...

4
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:28,695
Sir, I've never even been to college.
I swear.

5
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:33,074
I think that our lines got crossed.
I'm sorry.

6
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,712
You're not Korean, are you?

7
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:56,221
Here.

8
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:57,307
Thank you.

9
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:06,024
I managed to come over from the North
and started working here.

10
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:09,444
They told me...

11
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:13,531
if I worked for them,
they'd give me a registration card.

12
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:15,116
Eventually.

13
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:18,536
Right.

14
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:29,088
Would you be interested in working here?

15
00:01:29,089 --> 00:01:30,465
Mm-hmm.

16
00:01:36,679 --> 00:01:39,140
- Hey. Seo Hyun-tae.
- Y-Yes?

17
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:41,017
Where are you from?

18
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:46,064
Look at me.

19
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:49,776
North Korea? China? The Soviet Union?

20
00:01:50,527 --> 00:01:52,695
Wherever it is, you can't go back,
can you?

21
00:01:59,619 --> 00:02:00,995
Do not fear, okay.

22
00:02:02,831 --> 00:02:04,249
Do not fear.

23
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:10,964
I'm hungry.

24
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:13,383
When's he gonna wake up?

25
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:23,203
THE BLUE ROAD

26
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:47,769
Mommy, look at this.

27
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:01,658
Inose.

28
00:04:02,825 --> 00:04:04,285
You were taken too soon.

29
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:06,371
I still can't believe it.

30
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:10,917
We will feel this deep sorrow
in our hearts forever.

31
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:15,838
We will never heal from the tragedy
of losing a precious colleague.

32
00:04:17,173 --> 00:04:18,799
On behalf of all of us
at the police department...

33
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,217
Look. It's the Korean detective.

34
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:22,219
He's got some nerve, showing up here.

35
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:24,179
I hear those drug
trafficking charges against him

36
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,264
were all dropped.

37
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,473
What the hell?

38
00:04:26,474 --> 00:04:28,767
Doesn't he realize
he's the reason Inose is dead?

39
00:04:28,768 --> 00:04:29,978
Shh. Quiet.

40
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:33,189
Inose, my comrade, may you rest in peace.

41
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:54,794
Miss? Excuse me.

42
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:00,967
Oh.

43
00:05:02,176 --> 00:05:04,762
You're... Kim Seok, right?

44
00:05:05,596 --> 00:05:06,597
Yes.

45
00:05:09,475 --> 00:05:10,727
I wanted to tell you...

46
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:14,397
I am so sorry for your loss.

47
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:22,322
Damn right you're sorry, you should be.

48
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:27,327
How am I supposed to
afford Rumi's tuition now?

49
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:34,625
What? You think I'm being callous?

50
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:37,587
- Despite us being divorced?
- No.

51
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:40,340
No, I don't think that at all.

52
00:05:42,675 --> 00:05:45,345
And I'm sure that Inose is sorry as well.

53
00:05:45,928 --> 00:05:48,097
Mister, did you fall down?

54
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:53,852
Don't worry about it.

55
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:56,898
All this going back and forth
between Korea and Hong Kong...

56
00:05:57,523 --> 00:05:59,817
Who did he think he was, Superman?

57
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,528
I don't know if it was for you...

58
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:06,866
or if he felt a sense of duty
as a detective...

59
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:15,958
Being a detective is a horrible career
for anyone.

60
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:20,797
Last thing...

61
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:32,350
He wanted you two to have this.

62
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:11,139
Huh?

63
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:33,744
OLD CITY

64
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:56,850
<i>Attention, ladies and gentlemen.</i>

65
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:59,436
- Can I get a coffee, please?
- Is it on time?

66
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:01,981
- Two milk, no sugar.
- Okay, good. We're not late.

67
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:06,402
<i>Do not touch it yourself.</i>

68
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:10,780
<i>As a reminder, smoking is not permitted
inside the train terminal.</i>

69
00:08:10,781 --> 00:08:12,909
<i>Please use the designated smoking area.</i>

70
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:16,913
<i>The next train will depart on the
North track in approximately ten minutes.</i>

71
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,706
<i>Have all tickets out.</i>

72
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:50,363
Dandelion Village?

73
00:08:54,158 --> 00:08:56,786
You gonna kill someone there?
What for, revenge?

74
00:08:58,996 --> 00:09:00,122
You Japanese? Chinese?

75
00:09:00,706 --> 00:09:02,041
He said he's Korean.

76
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:05,044
Korean?

77
00:09:07,004 --> 00:09:08,214
Anastasia!

78
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,721
You're gonna give him a ride
to Dandelion Village.

79
00:09:16,847 --> 00:09:18,432
Your mom is Koryo-saram, right?

80
00:09:20,851 --> 00:09:22,311
Not the one who raised me.

81
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:23,813
My birth mom.

82
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:29,360
Whatever. You speak Korean, right?

83
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:32,822
She'll be your driver.

84
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:40,663
By the way...

85
00:09:41,872 --> 00:09:44,917
don't fuck with her.

86
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:46,711
This way, let's go.

87
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:00,891
Why are you looking at me like that?

88
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:04,186
You just look like someone I know.

89
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,816
So, you speak Korean.

90
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:11,485
Where did you learn it?

91
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:16,699
From my mother.

92
00:10:18,909 --> 00:10:20,286
My mom always said...

93
00:10:21,746 --> 00:10:23,289
one day we'd return to Korea.

94
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:25,875
And that when we did...

95
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:28,210
we needed to know our own language.

96
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:31,005
So you're going to Korea?

97
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:33,883
My mother died.

98
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:36,636
So, no.

99
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:39,055
Korea was never our home.

100
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:41,807
We don't have a home of our own.

101
00:10:58,074 --> 00:10:59,575
A friend from the Blue Road.

102
00:11:05,456 --> 00:11:06,749
The Blue Road, huh?

103
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,087
Or in the Koryo language...

104
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:15,257
<i>The Blue Road.</i>

105
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:22,807
Our ancestors, the people of Joseon...

106
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:25,184
they were pushed here

107
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:27,395
from Joseon.

108
00:11:29,313 --> 00:11:30,773
Driven out of their homes.

109
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:33,651
They were forced to leave everything.

110
00:11:34,443 --> 00:11:36,028
Shocked by the freezing cold.

111
00:11:37,697 --> 00:11:38,698
And as they walked...

112
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:42,410
they cried.

113
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:45,246
They wept big, heavy tears.

114
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:50,543
Weeping all along the road.

115
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:54,171
Became blue with their tears.

116
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:58,259
The Blue Road.

117
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,437
The Blue Road.

118
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:30,666
Still three more hours
until we reach Dandelion Village.

119
00:12:31,751 --> 00:12:33,377
There's nowhere to sleep there, you know.

120
00:12:34,086 --> 00:12:35,504
No one lives there anymore.

121
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:37,840
So, tonight, we'll sleep here.

122
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:45,222
All that's left now

123
00:12:46,807 --> 00:12:48,267
are graves and bandits.

124
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,273
Yeah, that's why I'm here.

125
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:53,290
I'm sorry.

126
00:14:04,093 --> 00:14:05,094
Stop!

127
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:56,020
Hey.

128
00:15:02,234 --> 00:15:03,903
Hey there.

129
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:07,281
I've risen from the dead,
just like Jesus did.

130
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:18,876
<i>Inose? That really you?</i>

131
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:21,670
Yes. It's me.

132
00:15:23,255 --> 00:15:26,507
And you're Chief Shimizu
of Investigation Division One.

133
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:30,762
After three years without a single
promotion, you drank a bottle of liquor

134
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:33,474
<i>and threw up all over my carpet. Remember?</i>

135
00:15:36,393 --> 00:15:37,603
Oh, my gosh. It is you!

136
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:39,562
Listen, no time to explain.

137
00:15:39,563 --> 00:15:41,064
I need your help, Chief.

138
00:15:41,065 --> 00:15:42,524
It's time to catch Ito.

139
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:45,861
I'll do whatever you need.

140
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:50,406
All right, everybody. We're resetting.

141
00:15:50,407 --> 00:15:52,200
What are you doing? You can't be here!

142
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:54,369
This is the police!
Cease what you're doing.

143
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,496
- What the hell is going on?
- Hey, you got a warrant?

144
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:58,457
- What do you think you're doing here?
- Who let them in?

145
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:03,252
After all the complaints made against you
for slander,

146
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:05,755
you think you have a right
to ask for a warrant?

147
00:16:05,756 --> 00:16:07,799
'Cause I can absolutely bring one
if you want.

148
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:10,718
No, no, hold on.
That... that's not what I meant.

149
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:13,179
Oh. since you didn't mean that,

150
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:15,682
then you'll have no problem
offering up your show?

151
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:19,853
This tragedy was so horrible,
killed in the line of duty.

152
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:24,608
And in addition to all that,

153
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:29,237
the Korean detective who worked
on the case with him was so traumatized

154
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:31,824
he left the police force altogether.

155
00:16:34,284 --> 00:16:35,953
So if

156
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:39,790
a rumor goes around that I'm dead
and Kim Seok left the force,

157
00:16:40,624 --> 00:16:42,209
Seo Hyun-tae will come out of hiding.

158
00:16:44,211 --> 00:16:47,296
And then he'll bring Speed K back out
on the streets again.

159
00:16:47,297 --> 00:16:49,258
This whole thing is crazy.

160
00:16:52,302 --> 00:16:53,470
Chief.

161
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:56,265
They had this.

162
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,729
What is this?
We haven't seen this in ages.

163
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:06,691
Hey. Where did you get this?

164
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:09,820
<i>Korean National Intelligence
Service will trace it back to the source.</i>

165
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:17,494
There's a hospital
three kilometers from here.

166
00:17:18,245 --> 00:17:19,580
A police station too.

167
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:21,749
Step on it.

168
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:25,794
Go. Go!

169
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:36,638
You know Ito's figured it out.

170
00:17:38,474 --> 00:17:40,476
We gotta hurry.

171
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:54,156
Please... please don't hurt me.

172
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:10,214
I know. She looks like her.

173
00:18:17,846 --> 00:18:18,931
I'm sorry.

174
00:18:20,682 --> 00:18:24,812
Are you okay?
I mean, have you been injured?

175
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:27,606
Oh.

176
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:29,942
Thank God.

177
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,783
It's dangerous.
You should go back a different way.

178
00:18:40,452 --> 00:18:41,995
If you ever do go to Korea...

179
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:45,541
you can reach me here.

180
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:51,463
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY
INSPECTOR KIM SEOK

181
00:18:54,716 --> 00:18:55,926
Let's go.

182
00:19:25,747 --> 00:19:28,917
This here is an Interpol operation
to catch our guy.

183
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:33,005
But we can't kill him.

184
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:36,842
No matter what he tries.

185
00:19:38,719 --> 00:19:40,470
You can't forget your duty as a cop.

186
00:19:58,488 --> 00:19:59,907
Kim Seok!

187
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:03,619
You're a police officer!

188
00:20:10,167 --> 00:20:11,585
I'm gonna remember that now.

189
00:20:31,855 --> 00:20:34,066
DANDELION CEMETERY

190
00:20:46,995 --> 00:20:47,996
Uh-huh.

191
00:20:50,165 --> 00:20:55,920
- Stop! You're hurting me!
- Hey, what is it? Move, you're too tall!

192
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,673
I can rub it around in my hands.

193
00:21:10,018 --> 00:21:11,436
Look who it is.

194
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,438
It's been a minute.

195
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:21,363
Kids present.

196
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:32,623
- It's nice to meet you
- Are you guys cops?

197
00:21:32,624 --> 00:21:34,543
Are they police officers?
Why are they here?

198
00:21:35,544 --> 00:21:36,545
Arrest you!

199
00:21:41,341 --> 00:21:42,342
Igor.

200
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,260
Makoto.

201
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:45,345
Hyun-tae.

202
00:21:47,389 --> 00:21:49,349
All those names are me.

203
00:21:54,062 --> 00:21:55,897
So many of our compatriots...

204
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:59,109
died here, in misery.

205
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:03,864
My father, my grandfather.

206
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:08,076
They were dragged here from their homeland
during the Japanese occupation.

207
00:22:09,494 --> 00:22:11,163
Brought here for no reason.

208
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:13,874
But I managed to survive.

209
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:17,252
Like a dandelion.

210
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:25,427
And?

211
00:22:27,346 --> 00:22:29,806
So, does that make you a victim
who needs to be rescued?

212
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:34,770
Someone who had no choice but
to distribute drugs in a place like this?

213
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:37,606
Follow me.

214
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:02,839
Ito.

215
00:23:04,674 --> 00:23:06,051
I'm placing you under arrest.

216
00:23:06,676 --> 00:23:08,637
You're charged with murder,
soliciting violence,

217
00:23:09,304 --> 00:23:11,390
- unlawful disposal of a body--
- Didn't you come here...

218
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:15,435
to find out what really happened?

219
00:23:21,733 --> 00:23:24,486
I've already figured it all out,
so no need to explain.

220
00:23:29,116 --> 00:23:32,743
Whatever Hong Du-yeong did,
it has nothing to do with me no, so...

221
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:35,205
Kim Seok, you truly are obsessed,
aren't you?

222
00:23:36,623 --> 00:23:38,208
He wasn't even your father.

223
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:40,502
Although, I suppose...

224
00:23:41,002 --> 00:23:44,756
Hong Du-yeong did look after you
and your mom, right up until he died.

225
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:52,389
MUNHWA THEATER 1
MUNHWA THEATER 2

226
00:23:52,889 --> 00:23:55,850
I heard that Mr. Minamoto
went to Japan after he retired.

227
00:23:55,851 --> 00:23:57,561
And that you're living in Gunsan.

228
00:23:58,770 --> 00:23:59,771
It's true.

229
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:02,482
He, uh, was granted some state land.

230
00:24:03,859 --> 00:24:08,363
He's planning to build a pharmaceutical
factory as part of the family business.

231
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:11,199
If he tried to build one in Japan,

232
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:14,035
there would've been complaints
about pollution.

233
00:24:21,251 --> 00:24:22,251
Shunsuke.

234
00:24:22,252 --> 00:24:23,335
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
SEO HYUN-TAE

235
00:24:23,336 --> 00:24:24,588
Go play outside for a bit.

236
00:24:28,049 --> 00:24:29,676
All right, Du-yeong. Let's go in.

237
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:50,489
He's Mr. Minamoto's son.

238
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:53,116
I'm taking care of him.

239
00:24:55,243 --> 00:24:56,745
I couldn't leave him all alone.

240
00:25:11,885 --> 00:25:15,347
So, they want you to kill me
for your registration card?

241
00:25:19,309 --> 00:25:21,353
Don't seem too worried about it, though.

242
00:25:25,524 --> 00:25:27,108
I get it now.

243
00:25:28,860 --> 00:25:30,820
All those things you and I did...

244
00:25:32,405 --> 00:25:34,324
we'll never be forgiven for them.

245
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:53,552
What was that?

246
00:25:58,848 --> 00:26:00,976
You know, I've been so happy lately.

247
00:26:01,643 --> 00:26:03,019
And I realize...

248
00:26:04,437 --> 00:26:09,776
forgiveness isn't in the cards for us.

249
00:26:12,904 --> 00:26:14,573
You've been happy lately?

250
00:26:28,962 --> 00:26:30,380
Tell me that you're joking.

251
00:26:53,194 --> 00:26:54,571
Then die, motherfucker.

252
00:26:57,824 --> 00:26:58,825
You...

253
00:26:59,534 --> 00:27:02,537
What the hell...

254
00:27:04,205 --> 00:27:06,166
do we need forgiveness for?

255
00:27:09,169 --> 00:27:10,670
Please, don't...

256
00:27:12,839 --> 00:27:13,965
Just please...

257
00:27:14,799 --> 00:27:17,010
not the kid or his mother.

258
00:27:19,220 --> 00:27:21,221
You bastard, die!

259
00:27:21,222 --> 00:27:22,307
You son of a bitch.

260
00:28:06,643 --> 00:28:07,644
<i>Emiri.</i>

261
00:28:13,483 --> 00:28:15,443
<i>And?</i>

262
00:28:17,070 --> 00:28:18,488
What are you telling me this for?

263
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:24,452
My duty as an officer is to arrest
some stupid bastard who murdered people.

264
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:28,415
Get up.

265
00:28:29,582 --> 00:28:31,918
You think your real father
went missing, right?

266
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:36,548
What did you just say?

267
00:28:38,133 --> 00:28:39,759
- Enough.
- One minute.

268
00:28:40,427 --> 00:28:41,720
Just arrest him.

269
00:28:43,346 --> 00:28:44,431
What are you doing?

270
00:28:47,016 --> 00:28:48,059
What is it?

271
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:49,978
What are you afraid of?

272
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:00,280
Come on. Tell me.

273
00:29:15,837 --> 00:29:17,464
Before we retired...

274
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:20,591
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
HONG DU-YEONG

275
00:29:20,592 --> 00:29:22,010
Check it out.

276
00:29:25,472 --> 00:29:27,390
I'm officially a Korean citizen.

277
00:29:28,391 --> 00:29:30,643
How did this happen? How?

278
00:29:31,519 --> 00:29:33,187
When did they give you this?

279
00:29:33,188 --> 00:29:35,899
Don't worry. They'll get you yours soon.

280
00:29:37,942 --> 00:29:40,361
Word's going around
the Print business is closing shop.

281
00:29:41,529 --> 00:29:42,655
It's closing shop?

282
00:29:46,075 --> 00:29:47,576
With the Olympics coming up,

283
00:29:47,577 --> 00:29:50,412
the influx of travel,
tourists coming in from all over,

284
00:29:50,413 --> 00:29:52,290
- they want to get rid of people like us.
- Wait a minute.

285
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:54,208
Wh-What about my ID?

286
00:29:54,209 --> 00:29:55,709
Don't be so high-strung.

287
00:29:55,710 --> 00:29:57,796
Hey. You'll get one.

288
00:29:59,547 --> 00:30:01,800
You know too much for them not to, okay?

289
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:05,011
Just be patient.

290
00:30:09,098 --> 00:30:10,600
So if they close the Print Shop,

291
00:30:11,976 --> 00:30:13,061
what will you do?

292
00:30:13,853 --> 00:30:17,065
Oh, me? I've got a plan.

293
00:30:21,236 --> 00:30:23,071
Check her out. She's pretty, huh?

294
00:30:28,201 --> 00:30:29,202
What is that?

295
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:36,876
<i>Oh...</i>

296
00:30:38,086 --> 00:30:39,671
<i>I found it in his wallet.</i>

297
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:46,344
<i>I'm thinking of paying his house a visit.</i>

298
00:30:49,597 --> 00:30:51,766
<i>Imagine how lonely his widow must be.</i>

299
00:30:52,559 --> 00:30:54,102
<i>I feel terrible for her.</i>

300
00:30:55,311 --> 00:30:58,147
I mean, who knows?
Maybe we'll all live together.

301
00:31:01,484 --> 00:31:03,528
After all, we gotta keep living.

302
00:31:06,823 --> 00:31:08,032
You've lost your mind.

303
00:31:08,783 --> 00:31:09,951
Hmm?

304
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:12,745
Have you gone completely insane?

305
00:31:16,291 --> 00:31:19,002
Were any of us ever really sane?

306
00:31:22,547 --> 00:31:24,591
<i>He wasn't missing.</i>

307
00:31:25,508 --> 00:31:27,802
Hong Du-yeong buried your father
in the hills,

308
00:31:28,636 --> 00:31:30,179
so no one would ever find him.

309
00:31:33,391 --> 00:31:34,392
How about that?

310
00:31:35,435 --> 00:31:36,853
Isn't that a cool story?

311
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:42,149
He really was something, wasn't he?

312
00:31:42,150 --> 00:31:43,234
Right?

313
00:31:44,819 --> 00:31:46,863
He saw a pretty woman in a photo...

314
00:31:49,032 --> 00:31:51,701
...from the wallet of a man he'd murdered.

315
00:31:56,122 --> 00:31:57,915
- Hmm?
- Kim Seok!

316
00:31:57,916 --> 00:32:00,334
- And he went all that way.
- Keep it up, I dare you.

317
00:32:00,335 --> 00:32:01,710
He's trying to play you! Kim Seok, stop!

318
00:32:01,711 --> 00:32:03,546
That man got what he deserved.

319
00:32:05,465 --> 00:32:06,633
Look at me.

320
00:32:07,133 --> 00:32:08,258
Kim Seok!

321
00:32:08,259 --> 00:32:10,053
Look at me when I'm talking.

322
00:32:11,095 --> 00:32:13,055
Too much for you?

323
00:32:13,056 --> 00:32:14,140
Shut up.

324
00:32:15,099 --> 00:32:17,560
- That's enough!
- Inose.

325
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:34,202
Don't worry. It won't kill him.

326
00:32:44,087 --> 00:32:45,713
This is more important.

327
00:32:50,969 --> 00:32:52,845
What are you doing?

328
00:32:58,226 --> 00:32:59,811
Well, your mother has to be told.

329
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:08,403
Waiting for your command.

330
00:33:15,576 --> 00:33:19,247
Who... who... who are you?

331
00:33:21,290 --> 00:33:23,376
<i>Are you really a friend of Seok?</i>

332
00:33:24,794 --> 00:33:25,837
<i>Seok?</i>

333
00:33:26,587 --> 00:33:28,006
<i>I'm scared, Seok.</i>

334
00:33:29,215 --> 00:33:30,717
Du-yeong.

335
00:33:32,176 --> 00:33:34,012
Du-yeong.

336
00:33:35,930 --> 00:33:38,181
<i>Where are you, Du-yeong?</i>

337
00:33:38,182 --> 00:33:40,183
<i>Where did you go?</i>

338
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:41,769
- <i>Du-yeong!</i>
- Just stand by for now.

339
00:33:43,354 --> 00:33:44,355
Well?

340
00:33:46,107 --> 00:33:48,776
Is it time to explain
that the very man who saved her...

341
00:33:50,528 --> 00:33:52,780
actually murdered her husband
and took his place?

342
00:33:54,824 --> 00:33:56,492
What do you think she'll say to that?

343
00:33:58,703 --> 00:34:01,247
- <i>Du-yeong. Du-yeong.</i>
- Shall we tell her?

344
00:34:05,376 --> 00:34:07,128
I'm not sure she'll be able to take it.

345
00:34:08,463 --> 00:34:10,840
Considering how fragile
her health is already.

346
00:34:14,177 --> 00:34:15,178
Well?

347
00:34:17,597 --> 00:34:20,224
Should she find out? Huh?

348
00:34:21,100 --> 00:34:22,559
<i>Du-yeong...</i>

349
00:34:22,560 --> 00:34:25,521
<i>Du-yeong, why did you leave me?</i>

350
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:29,233
You win. I'll stop. Okay?

351
00:34:30,359 --> 00:34:32,195
I was wrong. I admit it.

352
00:34:34,655 --> 00:34:35,740
Just stop now.

353
00:34:46,042 --> 00:34:47,335
What should I do now?

354
00:34:50,505 --> 00:34:51,631
Any ideas?

355
00:34:56,803 --> 00:34:58,054
I'm so sorry.

356
00:34:58,721 --> 00:35:00,139
Please forgive me, please.

357
00:35:01,766 --> 00:35:03,643
Oh, please forgive me.

358
00:35:09,315 --> 00:35:10,566
Mu-seong, what's going on?

359
00:35:14,570 --> 00:35:15,822
Mu-seong. Answer me.

360
00:35:16,572 --> 00:35:18,032
What's going on over there?

361
00:35:21,702 --> 00:35:25,080
Shh. Let's just go quietly. Yeah?

362
00:35:25,081 --> 00:35:26,165
<i>Mu-seong!</i>

363
00:35:33,881 --> 00:35:35,091
You're safe now.

364
00:35:36,467 --> 00:35:38,052
Everything's all right, ma'am.

365
00:35:42,306 --> 00:35:43,432
Kim Seok, you there?

366
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:47,145
Your mother is safe.

367
00:36:06,330 --> 00:36:09,333
I'll go. I'll go.

368
00:36:10,001 --> 00:36:11,002
You stay.

369
00:36:55,046 --> 00:36:56,297
I have to end this.

370
00:36:57,673 --> 00:36:58,925
I have to.

371
00:37:30,748 --> 00:37:32,917
We're finishing this. Enough.

372
00:37:38,923 --> 00:37:40,132
This ends now.

373
00:38:02,989 --> 00:38:03,990
Do it.

374
00:38:05,616 --> 00:38:06,701
Just kill me.

375
00:38:11,330 --> 00:38:12,873
Unless you're too scared.

376
00:38:18,879 --> 00:38:19,880
No.

377
00:38:21,382 --> 00:38:22,383
I'm not scared.

378
00:38:27,513 --> 00:38:28,514
Kim Seok!

379
00:38:33,519 --> 00:38:34,520
Don't do it!

380
00:38:40,443 --> 00:38:41,444
Don't!

381
00:38:42,820 --> 00:38:43,946
Drop the gun!

382
00:38:52,663 --> 00:38:53,747
We're the police.

383
00:38:53,748 --> 00:38:55,249
We're detectives!

384
00:38:57,793 --> 00:38:59,920
You can't just kill whoever you want!

385
00:39:00,796 --> 00:39:03,549
Our job is to bring him in
and let the law decide!

386
00:39:04,342 --> 00:39:05,343
Kim Seok.

387
00:39:06,802 --> 00:39:08,053
Kim Seok!

388
00:39:08,054 --> 00:39:09,430
You are afraid.

389
00:39:11,140 --> 00:39:12,850
You're so scared right now.

390
00:39:15,936 --> 00:39:17,563
- Kim Seok!
- I can see it.

391
00:39:38,584 --> 00:39:39,752
Do not fear.

392
00:39:49,637 --> 00:39:50,638
Do not fear.

393
00:40:36,809 --> 00:40:39,103
Kim Seok? Kim Seok!

394
00:40:39,812 --> 00:40:42,105
Hey, Kim Seok!

395
00:40:42,106 --> 00:40:43,190
You hear me?

396
00:40:45,484 --> 00:40:46,569
You're okay.

397
00:40:47,736 --> 00:40:48,779
You'll be okay.

398
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:51,281
Look at me.

399
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:52,365
Kim Seok!

400
00:40:52,366 --> 00:40:53,617
Look at me.

401
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:56,453
Kim Seok.

402
00:40:56,454 --> 00:40:57,538
Inose.

403
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:02,209
I've done...

404
00:41:04,044 --> 00:41:05,880
so many bad things in my life.

405
00:41:08,674 --> 00:41:09,675
Still...

406
00:41:12,803 --> 00:41:13,929
because of you...

407
00:41:17,600 --> 00:41:19,477
I made everything right in the end.

408
00:41:22,730 --> 00:41:23,939
As a detective.

409
00:41:26,901 --> 00:41:27,901
You'll be okay.

410
00:41:27,902 --> 00:41:29,528
Thank you. Really.

411
00:41:30,070 --> 00:41:31,071
Kim Seok!

412
00:42:42,560 --> 00:42:44,812
Right, let's move on to our final case.

413
00:42:47,064 --> 00:42:48,065
Whoa.

414
00:42:51,443 --> 00:42:52,695
That's really something.

415
00:42:55,739 --> 00:42:58,075
I know these photographs
might be tough to look at.

416
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:03,330
They pertain to a murder case
that took place in Japan back in 2002.

417
00:43:04,957 --> 00:43:07,209
The crime scene was especially complex.

418
00:43:07,835 --> 00:43:09,961
As you can see,
text was left at the scene.

419
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:12,255
ONE FEAR GIVES BIRTH TO ENDLESS FEARS,
BUT ITS METHODS SHALL REMAIN HIDDEN.

420
00:43:12,256 --> 00:43:15,050
The body was arranged
in a very particular manner.

421
00:43:18,220 --> 00:43:19,512
I think I heard about this case.

422
00:43:19,513 --> 00:43:25,394
So, tell me...
who could have devised a method like this?

423
00:43:26,729 --> 00:43:27,730
Why?

424
00:43:29,023 --> 00:43:30,857
How did they make it happen?

425
00:43:30,858 --> 00:43:32,609
It's gotta be some real deviant.

426
00:43:32,610 --> 00:43:34,528
Who could come up
with something like that?

427
00:43:35,112 --> 00:43:36,447
Was it all by design?

428
00:43:37,364 --> 00:43:41,452
Or was it an accident
that spiraled out of proportion?

429
00:43:51,253 --> 00:43:53,005
They did catch the guy in the end.

430
00:44:01,764 --> 00:44:06,894
GOVERNMENT EMPLOYEE IDKIM GONG-JU

431
00:44:10,356 --> 00:44:11,523
You've done well.

432
00:44:12,191 --> 00:44:13,192
Oh, please.

433
00:44:15,903 --> 00:44:18,364
I've got you to thank. Well, both of you.

434
00:44:29,375 --> 00:44:31,460
I'm a little embarrassed to say this, but...

435
00:44:32,419 --> 00:44:33,712
Hmm? What?

436
00:44:35,464 --> 00:44:37,090
To be honest,

437
00:44:37,091 --> 00:44:38,676
I'd completely forgotten
you were coming today.

438
00:44:39,593 --> 00:44:40,636
"Forgotten"?

439
00:44:41,387 --> 00:44:43,889
Ah, it means forgot.

440
00:44:48,435 --> 00:44:51,730
I've still got a lot of Korean to learn.

441
00:45:17,923 --> 00:45:20,926
KIM SEOK'S GRAVE

442
00:45:42,448 --> 00:45:44,283
It's hard to believe how long it's been.

443
00:45:50,748 --> 00:45:51,749
Even so...

444
00:45:53,667 --> 00:45:54,793
we have to remember.

445
00:46:00,883 --> 00:46:02,050
Just 'cause it's over...

446
00:46:07,723 --> 00:46:08,932
it doesn't mean we can forget.

447
00:46:31,497 --> 00:46:32,498
I'm sorry.

448
00:47:23,173 --> 00:47:24,508
You did good, Inose.

449
00:47:34,768 --> 00:47:35,769
Good job.

450
00:47:43,694 --> 00:47:44,695
Ha!

451
00:48:03,213 --> 00:48:04,214
What?

452
00:48:14,766 --> 00:48:15,766
I won't forget.

453
00:48:15,767 --> 00:48:16,852
Hmm.
